      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect \u2014 I found exactly what you\u0027re asking about.\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never holding it there at all.** Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the child process environment** \u2014 either the Ingest or Query agent \u2014 immediately before that child process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key by inspecting its own environment variables, because the key never exists there. The credential only lives inside the short-lived child process that actually makes calls to the Anthropic API.\n\nThis same scoping model applies to both the Ingest and Query agents \u2014 each receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from the Hub.\n\nSource: [[credential-scoping]]",
      "input_tokens": 5378,
      "output_tokens": 223
    }
